I walk to the market exit.
Suddenly, I get a very good smell.
It is fresh jasmine.
A woman is sitting on a mat there.
She is making jasmine strings.
I go near her.
"Chechi, please give me a small jasmine string," I say.
The woman smiles at me.
She gives a flower string to me.
The flowers are very beautiful.
"What is the price for this?" I ask.
"Thirty rupees," the woman says.
I take money from my bag.
I give her thirty rupees.
The woman takes the money.
"Thank you," she says.
I put that jasmine in my bag.
